---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { url } from '../lib/url'
import plugins from '../data/plugins.json'

// Only adapters the sandbox has a platform double for, commerce first: they exercise the most.
const order = ['shopify', 'woocommerce', 'onetrust']
const runnable = order
  .map((name) => plugins.find((plugin) => plugin.name === name))
  .filter((plugin) => plugin !== undefined)

const fixtureSources = [...new Set(runnable.flatMap((p) => p.fixtures.map((f) => f.source).filter(Boolean)))]
---

<Base
  title="Sandbox"
  description="Run the real adapters against recorded platform payloads in your browser and watch exactly which RUM calls they make."
>
  <h1>Sandbox</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This runs the <strong>real adapters</strong>, from the same published builds you would install,
    against the <strong>same recorded payloads the test suite uses</strong>. It records the RUM calls
    each adapter makes instead of sending them, and shows you every one.
  </p>

  <p class="notice">
    <strong>Nothing leaves your browser and no Datadog account is involved.</strong> The sandbox never
    initializes RUM and never asks for an application ID or client token. Recording the calls rather
    than sending them is also the only way to show the parts that matter most — the consent gate
    holding events back, a second order being refused, card data being stripped — because in all
    three cases the correct behaviour is that <em>nothing is sent at all</em>.
  </p>

  <div class="sandbox" data-sandbox>
    <div class="sandbox-controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="adapter">Adapter</label>
        <select id="adapter">
          {runnable.map((plugin, index) => (
            <option value={plugin.name} selected={index === 0}>{plugin.title ?? plugin.name}</option>
          ))}
        </select>
      </div>

      <fieldset data-commerce-only>
        <legend>Options</legend>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-option="includeItems" /> <code>includeItems</code></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-option="includeEmail" /> <code>includeEmail</code></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-option="includeName" /> <code>includeName</code></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" data-option="identifyUsers" checked /> <code>identifyUsers</code></label>
        <label>
          <input type="checkbox" data-option="consentIgnore" />
          <code>consent: 'ignore'</code>
          <span class="small muted">— skip the gate, as if a consent plugin already granted</span>
        </label>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="field" data-shopify-only>
        <label for="privacy">Shopify Customer Privacy API</label>
        <select id="privacy">
          <option value="absent" selected>Not present (pixel sandbox)</option>
          <option value="allowed">analyticsProcessingAllowed() → true</option>
          <option value="denied">analyticsProcessingAllowed() → false</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="field" data-onetrust-only hidden>
        <label for="category">Required OneTrust category</label>
        <input id="category" type="text" value="C0002" spellcheck="false" />
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="prefix">Action prefix</label>
        <input id="prefix" type="text" value="commerce." spellcheck="false" />
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="button" data-run-all>Run every step</button>
        <button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
      </div>

      <p class="small muted" data-status></p>
    </div>

    <div class="sandbox-steps">
      <h2>Steps</h2>
      <p class="small muted">
        Fire them one at a time, or run them all. Each is a payload recorded from the real platform.
      </p>
      <ol class="step-list" data-steps></ol>
    </div>

    <div class="sandbox-output">
      <h2>RUM calls</h2>
      <p class="small muted">
        What the adapter asked the SDK to do, in order. An entry in red is something the core
        refused to send, with the reason.
      </p>
      <div class="log" data-log aria-live="polite">
        <p class="muted small">Fire a step to see the calls.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Things worth trying</h2>

  <h3>The refusals</h3>
  <p>
    These are the behaviours a live demo cannot show, because in each case the correct outcome is
    that nothing is sent. The adapters run with <code>debug: true</code>, so each refusal appears in
    the log with the core's own reason — the same output you get by following
    <a href={url('/docs/getting-started/')}>the verify step</a> on a real site.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Fire the order step twice</strong> (WooCommerce "order received", or Shopify's two
      <code>checkout_completed</code> steps — the second is a refreshed thank-you page). The second
      is refused: <code>commerce.purchase</code> fires once per <code>transaction_id</code>, which is
      what stops a reload double-counting revenue. <em>Reset</em> clears it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>WooCommerce with <code>consent: 'ignore'</code> off.</strong> Run every step: nothing is
      sent, not even <code>setUser</code>, and <code>trackingConsent</code> is set to
      <code>not-granted</code> before the SDK would start. Events during a pending decision are
      dropped rather than queued, so granting afterwards does not backfill them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shopify with the Customer Privacy API set to <code>false</code>.</strong> Same result,
      through the platform's own consent signal. Set it to <em>not present</em> and events flow —
      that is the pixel sandbox, where the Pixel Manager has already applied the merchant's
      categories before the pixel runs. Those three branches are the whole of Shopify's consent
      behaviour.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Narrow the action prefix, then watch a non-commerce action.</strong> Renaming commerce
      to <code>shop.</code> moves commerce actions only; <code>account.*</code> and
      <code>lead.*</code> keep their own prefix, so renaming commerce cannot silently rename a login.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What gets stripped</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Shopify's payment step and WooCommerce's order</strong> both carry a
      <code>card_number</code> in the recorded payload — WooCommerce's also carries a
      <code>billing_address</code>. Neither reaches the output. The fixtures carry them precisely so
      the stripping is exercised rather than assumed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shopify's search step</strong> sends <code>search_term_length: 14</code>. The query was
      "red tee medium"; the text never leaves the browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Turn <code>includeEmail</code> on.</strong> It appears on <code>setUser</code> and
      nowhere else — never on an action. Turn <code>identifyUsers</code> off and <code>setUser</code>
      stops entirely.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Consent, end to end</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Pick OneTrust and walk the steps in order.</strong> An unanswered banner reports
      nothing; reject-all reports <code>not-granted</code>; accepting performance grants; accepting
      everything is already granted, so it is not reported again; withdrawing denies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Change the required category to <code>C0004</code></strong> and walk them again. Now
      only the accept-everything step grants.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the payloads come from</h2>
  <ul class="small">
    {fixtureSources.map((source) => <li>{source}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p class="small muted">
    Live demos against a real Datadog organization live in the RUM playground site, linked from each
    plugin's page once the packages are published. This sandbox exists for the part a live demo
    cannot show: what an adapter refuses to send.
  </p>
  <p><a href={url('/plugins/')}>Browse the plugins →</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The site has no global [hidden] rule, and the display rules below would otherwise beat it. */
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }

  .sandbox {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    /* The site has no global [hidden] rule, and the display rules below would otherwise beat it. */
  [hidden] { display: none !important; }

  .sandbox { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .sandbox-controls, .sandbox-steps, .sandbox-output {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .sandbox-output { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / span 2; }
  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    .sandbox-output { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
  }
  .sandbox-controls .field { margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
  .sandbox-controls label { display: block; font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .sandbox-controls select, .sandbox-controls input[type='text'] {
    font: inherit;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  fieldset {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }
  legend { font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted); padding: 0 0.3rem; }
  fieldset label { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  fieldset input[type='checkbox'] { margin: 0; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .actions button, .step-list button {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .actions button[data-run-all] { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); border-color: transparent; }
  .actions button:hover, .step-list button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .step-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; counter-reset: s; }
  .step-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .step-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .step-list .step-name { flex: 1; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .step-list .step-event { font-size: 0.75rem; }

  .log { max-height: 34rem; overflow-y: auto; font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .log-entry { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.5rem 0; }
  .log-entry:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .log-api { font-weight: 650; }
  .log-blocked .log-api { color: #c0392b; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { .log-blocked .log-api { color: #ff8a7a; } }
  .log-entry pre { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; font-size: 0.75rem; }
  .log-step { font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.9rem 0 0.1rem; }
  .log-step:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
</style>

<script>
  import { clearDedupe, startSession, type SandboxAdapter, type SandboxCall, type SandboxFixture } from '../lib/sandbox'
  import plugins from '../data/plugins.json'

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sandbox]')
  if (root) {
    const adapterSelect = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#adapter')!
    const prefixInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#prefix')!
    const privacySelect = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#privacy')!
    const categoryInput = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#category')!
    const shopifyOnly = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-shopify-only]')!
    const onetrustOnly = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-onetrust-only]')!
    const stepList = root.querySelector<HTMLOListElement>('[data-steps]')!
    const log = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-log]')!
    const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!
    const optionInputs = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-option]')]

    type PluginData = { name: string; fixtures: SandboxFixture[] }
    const byName = new Map((plugins as PluginData[]).map((plugin) => [plugin.name, plugin]))

    let session: ReturnType<typeof startSession> | null = null

    const currentOptions = () => {
      const flags = Object.fromEntries(optionInputs.map((input) => [input.dataset.option, input.checked]))
      return {
        includeItems: flags.includeItems === true,
        includeEmail: flags.includeEmail === true,
        includeName: flags.includeName === true,
        identifyUsers: flags.identifyUsers === true,
        ...(flags.consentIgnore === true ? { consent: 'ignore' as const } : {}),
        actionPrefix: prefixInput.value || 'commerce.',
        shopifyPrivacy: privacySelect.value as 'absent' | 'allowed' | 'denied',
        category: categoryInput.value || 'C0002',
      }
    }

    /** Only show a control on the adapter it applies to. */
    function syncControls() {
      const adapter = adapterSelect.value
      shopifyOnly.hidden = adapter !== 'shopify'
      onetrustOnly.hidden = adapter !== 'onetrust'
      // A consent adapter emits no actions of its own, so the commerce options and the action
      // prefix mean nothing for it. Hide the whole fieldset rather than its labels, or the legend
      // is left behind as an empty box.
      const commerceOnly = adapter !== 'onetrust'
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-commerce-only]')!.hidden = !commerceOnly
      prefixInput.closest<HTMLElement>('.field')!.hidden = !commerceOnly
    }

    function appendStepHeading(text: string) {
      const heading = document.createElement('p')
      heading.className = 'log-step'
      heading.textContent = text
      log.append(heading)
      log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight
    }

    function appendCall(call: SandboxCall) {
      const entry = document.createElement('div')
      entry.className = call.blocked ? 'log-entry log-blocked' : 'log-entry'

      const head = document.createElement('div')
      const api = document.createElement('span')
      api.className = 'log-api'
      api.textContent = call.api
      head.append(api)

      if (call.label) {
        const label = document.createElement('code')
        label.textContent = ` ${call.label}`
        head.append(label)
      }
      if (call.blocked) {
        const reason = document.createElement('span')
        reason.className = 'muted small'
        reason.textContent = ` — ${call.blocked}`
        head.append(reason)
      }
      entry.append(head)

      if (call.detail !== undefined && Object.keys(call.detail as object ?? {}).length > 0) {
        const pre = document.createElement('pre')
        pre.textContent = JSON.stringify(call.detail, null, 2)
        entry.append(pre)
      }

      log.append(entry)
      log.scrollTop = log.scrollHeight
    }

    let callsThisStep = 0

    function reset({ keepDedupe = false } = {}) {
      log.replaceChildren()
      if (!keepDedupe) clearDedupe()
      // Options are read at init, so changing one rebuilds the adapter; stop the previous
      // session's console capture first or the forwarders stack up.
      session?.dispose()
      session = startSession(adapterSelect.value as SandboxAdapter, currentOptions(), (call) => {
        callsThisStep += 1
        appendCall(call)
      })

      const consentState = session.initConfiguration.trackingConsent
      status.textContent = session.initialized
        ? consentState
          ? `onInit ran. trackingConsent is "${consentState}", so nothing will be sent until consent is granted.`
          : 'onInit ran. The adapter left trackingConsent alone.'
        : 'The adapter opted out of this page (onInit returned false), so it subscribed to nothing.'
    }

    function renderSteps() {
      const plugin = byName.get(adapterSelect.value)
      stepList.replaceChildren()

      for (const fixture of plugin?.fixtures ?? []) {
        const item = document.createElement('li')

        const name = document.createElement('span')
        name.className = 'step-name'
        name.textContent = fixture.name
        if (fixture.description) name.title = fixture.description

        const event = document.createElement('code')
        event.className = 'step-event'
        event.textContent = fixture.event

        const fire = document.createElement('button')
        fire.type = 'button'
        fire.textContent = 'Fire'
        fire.addEventListener('click', () => {
          callsThisStep = 0
          appendStepHeading(fixture.name)
          session?.emit(fixture)
          if (callsThisStep === 0) {
            appendCall({ api: 'no RUM calls', blocked: 'the adapter sent nothing for this payload' })
          }
        })

        item.append(name, event, fire)
        stepList.append(item)
      }
    }

    root.querySelector('[data-run-all]')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
      reset()
      for (const fixture of byName.get(adapterSelect.value)?.fixtures ?? []) {
        callsThisStep = 0
        appendStepHeading(fixture.name)
        session?.emit(fixture)
        if (callsThisStep === 0) {
          appendCall({ api: 'no RUM calls', blocked: 'the adapter sent nothing for this payload' })
        }
      }
    })

    root.querySelector('[data-reset]')!.addEventListener('click', () => reset())

    adapterSelect.addEventListener('change', () => {
      syncControls()
      renderSteps()
      reset()
    })

    // Changing an option rebuilds the adapter, because options are read at init.
    for (const input of [...optionInputs, prefixInput, privacySelect, categoryInput]) {
      input.addEventListener('change', () => reset())
    }

    // Leave the console capture clean if the page goes away mid-session.
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => session?.dispose(), { once: true })

    syncControls()
    renderSteps()
    reset()
  }
</script>
